 {id:'compare',icon:'layout-column-line',name:'Compare concepts',tag:'DISTINGUISH',time:'5–8 min',line:'Find the difference that matters.',what:'Compare two related concepts while retaining the source context.',why:'An explicit distinction is easier to inspect than two disconnected definitions.',when:'When related terms or mechanisms are easy to confuse.',who:'Learners building a more precise mental model.',how:'Explain the first idea, name the second, state the useful difference, and verify both.',number:'2',unit:'ideas side by side',evidence:'Lumen guided practice · no clinical accuracy scoring'},
 {id:'visual',icon:'eye-off-line',name:'Visual recall',tag:'IDENTIFY',time:'3–5 min',line:'Hide. Name. Reveal.',what:'Cover a region on a study image and recall what is underneath.',why:'The exercise asks you to retrieve an image label rather than simply recognise it.',when:'With diagrams or source images you are authorised to study.',who:'Learners reviewing visual relationships or labels.',how:'Select an image collection, place or add a cover, name it, then reveal and check. Keyboard users can add a centre cover.',number:'20',unit:'covers per image, maximum',evidence:'Lumen tool limit · original image remains the reference'},
 {id:'evidence',icon:'shield-check-line',name:'Evidence lens',tag:'APPRAISE',time:'5–10 min',line:'Keep the claim and its limits together.',what:'A source-linked note separating a finding, a limitation, and your next question.',why:'A citation is easier to evaluate when the population, date, and uncertainty are visible.',when:'While reading research or comparing sources.',who:'Practitioners learning evidence appraisal; this is a learning template.',how:'Choose a source, record its page, write the claim and limits, then save an editable note.',number:'5',unit:'prompts for a better note',evidence:'Structured reflection · not a validated appraisal instrument'},
 {id:'return',icon:'history-line',name:'Spaced return',tag:'REVISIT',time:'Daily',line:'Let the schedule bring you back.',what:'Revisit cards at intervals based on your own recall rating.',why:'Scheduled review creates a clear next action instead of an undifferentiated pile of cards.',when:'When cards are ready; a rating of Again returns in 10 minutes.',who:'Learners maintaining a personal revision habit.',how:'Recall, reveal, then rate Again, Good, or Easy. Good advances one step; Easy advances two.',number:'6',unit:'intervals: 1 · 3 · 7 · 14 · 30 · 60 days',evidence:'Transparent Lumen ladder · not FSRS or a competency score'}
